[OK] Connected to Redis Cluster (attempt 1)

============================================================
  1. CACHE STAMPEDE  (hot key expires, many threads miss at once)
============================================================
  50 threads request the same key on an empty cache.
  Each DB query takes 300 ms.

  [PROBLEM: no protection  ] 50 threads -> DB calls:  50   wall time: 0.35s   errors: 0
  [FIXED:   SET NX lock    ] 50 threads -> DB calls:   1   wall time: 0.34s   errors: 0

  DB calls                 problem=50    fixed=1    (50.0x fewer)
  Result: PASS – only one thread rebuilt the cache

============================================================
  2. CACHE AVALANCHE  (many keys expire at the same time)
============================================================
  200 keys cached with a base TTL of 60s.

  [PROBLEM: identical TTL    ]  200 keys written in 0.03s
    expire in  60-64 s | ######################################## 200
    TTL range: 60s .. 60s   spread: 0s

  [FIXED:   TTL + jitter 0-30s]  200 keys written in 0.02s
    expire in  60-64 s | #######                                   34
    expire in  65-69 s | ######                                    28
    expire in  70-74 s | ######                                    28
    expire in  75-79 s | #######                                   32
    expire in  80-84 s | #######                                   35
    expire in  85-89 s | ########                                  36
    expire in  90-94 s | ##                                         7
    TTL range: 60s .. 90s   spread: 30s

  Max keys expiring/sec    problem=200    fixed=12    (16.7x fewer)
  Share of cache lost in the busiest second: 100% -> 6%
  Result: PASS – expiries are spread out, no mass expiry

============================================================
  3. CACHE PENETRATION  (requests for ids that do not exist)
============================================================
  100 requests for 10 non-existent ids (10 requests each).

  [PROBLEM: no null caching] 100 requests -> DB calls: 100   wall time: 5.11s   rows found: 0
  [FIXED:   null marker     ] 100 requests -> DB calls:  10   wall time: 0.56s   rows found: 0

  Null marker example: GET cp:item:900001 -> '__NULL__'  (TTL 30s)

  DB calls                 problem=100    fixed=10    (10.0x fewer)
  Result: PASS – only the first request per id hit the DB

